  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "Lisa D. Cook stated in September 2026 that she has long been an advocate of responsible AI development, from training data to AI safety. In the same speech, she said any specific government role in AI's trajectory is for elected officials to decide. In February 2026, she said that in her current role she has frequently spoken about AI advances, their economic implications, and the Fed's dual-mandate goals. She also expressed cautious long-run optimism about AI's innovation potential and described ways AI could boost productivity and broaden innovation.",
   "sids": [
    "s1",
    "s2",
    "s3",
    "s4",
    "s5",
    "s6"
   ],
   "sentences": [
    {
